      "arguments": "{\"patch\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/rohanvinaik/Projects/GSE/GSE/symbolic/lexical_grounding.py\\n@@\\n-        \\\"\\\"\\\"Unify a complete source frame, preserving finer identity uncertainty.\\n+        \\\"\\\"\\\"Unify a complete source frame as compatibility, not sense identity.\\n@@\\n-        Primary chart units are independently named meanings, not guesses at\\n-        the first ordinary dictionary reading. Only explicit catalogue native\\n-        alignments may select a native ID. Other units retain their canonical\\n-        chart ID and list the still-unresolved ordinary dictionary rivals.\\n-        The selected snapshot row -- never a frame's participants -- supplies\\n-        whatever partial values are actually admitted.\\n+        Primary chart units are independently named meanings. Their allowable\\n+        frames attest a possible use, not exclusion of ordinary meanings with\\n+        the same grammar (visual seeing versus consulting someone, for example).\\n+        Even an explicit catalogue alignment therefore cannot turn this match\\n+        into a selected row. Retain the exact source/role proof for concurrent\\n+        grounding, but assert no identity or bank from this witness alone.\\n@@\\n-            \\\"code\\\": \\\"PRIMARY_UNIT_FRAME\\\",\\n-            \\\"entry_id\\\": entry_id,\\n+            \\\"code\\\": \\\"PRIMARY_FRAME_COMPATIBLE_NOT_IDENTIFYING\\\",\\n+            \\\"compatible_entry_id\\\": entry_id,\\n             \\\"witness_kind\\\": \\\"NSM_PRIMARY_TYPED_FRAME\\\",\\n-            \\\"identity_scope\\\": \\\"EXPLICIT_NATIVE_ALIGNMENT\\\" if entry_id.startswith(\\\"wordnet:\\\") else \\\"PRIMARY_UNIT_ONLY\\\",\\n+            \\\"identity_scope\\\": \\\"UNRESOLVED\\\",\\n+            \\\"missing_witness\\\": \\\"INDEPENDENT_MEANING_DISCRIMINATION\\\",\\n*** Update File: /Users/rohanvinaik/Projects/GSE/GSE/api/encoder.py\\n@@\\n-                    if selection[\\\"code\\\"] in {\\\"EXACT_WORDNET_SENSE\\\", \\\"PRIMARY_UNIT_FRAME\\\"}:\\n+                    if selection[\\\"code\\\"] == \\\"EXACT_WORDNET_SENSE\\\":\\n*** Update File: /Users/rohanvinaik/Projects/GSE/GSE/symbolic/expression.py\\n@@\\n     modal = modal_primes([t.word_primitives for t in tokens if t.position < verb.position and t.pos == \\\"AUX\\\"])\\n     event = Op(primitive=verb.lemma, operation=\\\"EVENT\\\", arity=len(args), args=args, modal=modal)\\n+    # A bare post-verbal PP qualifies the event; it is not the verb's direct\\n+    # patient. Use the existing relation-over-event representation (also used\\n+    # for unresolved nominal prepositions), preserving BOTH the preposition\\n+    # and its anchor. Previously these constituents were silently discarded\\n+    # just because there was no object to put before them in EVENT.args.\\n+    if not object_atoms and len(obl_tokens) > 1:\\n+        event = Op(\\n+            primitive=obl_tokens[0].lemma,\\n+            operation=\\\"EVENT\\\",\\n+            arity=2,\\n+            args=[event, Phrase(atoms=[_atom_from_token(t, \\\"SYN_OBL\\\") for t in obl_tokens[1:]])],\\n+        )\\n     return Negation(operand=event) if negated else event\\n*** Update File: /Users/rohanvinaik/Projects/GSE/tests/test_runtime_native_identity_controls.py\\n@@\\n-    \\\"text,lemma,entry,scope\\\",\\n+    \\\"text,lemma,entry\\\",\\n@@\\n-        (\\\"You want something.\\\", \\\"want\\\", \\\"wordnet:want:desire.v.01\\\", \\\"EXPLICIT_NATIVE_ALIGNMENT\\\"),\\n-        (\\\"She thinks about something.\\\", \\\"think\\\", \\\"nsm_chart:v20:think\\\", \\\"PRIMARY_UNIT_ONLY\\\"),\\n-        (\\\"You know.\\\", \\\"know\\\", \\\"wordnet:know:know.v.01\\\", \\\"EXPLICIT_NATIVE_ALIGNMENT\\\"),\\n-        (\\\"I see someone.\\\", \\\"see\\\", \\\"wordnet:see:see.v.01\\\", \\\"EXPLICIT_NATIVE_ALIGNMENT\\\"),\\n-        (\\\"She hears something.\\\", \\\"hear\\\", \\\"wordnet:hear:hear.v.01\\\", \\\"EXPLICIT_NATIVE_ALIGNMENT\\\"),\\n-        (\